' ============================================================================
' Diagram A — Where this fits: Portal AuthN vs the existing Identity Provider
' connector. These are two genuinely separate systems that happen to both
' talk to Entra/Okta — this was the user's explicit design requirement.
' ============================================================================
@startuml A_context
title AccessPilot — Portal AuthN vs Identity Provider Connector (separate systems)

package "Existing (untouched this phase)" {
  [identity_providers table] as IDP
  [EntraProvider / OktaProvider connectors] as Connector
  [directory_sync.py\n(HR/user/group/role sync)] as Sync
  [provisioning.py\n(real account creation, birthright)] as Provisioning
  IDP --> Connector
  Connector --> Sync
  Connector --> Provisioning
}

package "New — Phase 12: Portal AuthN (who can log into AccessPilot itself)" {
  [bootstrap_credentials table] as BootstrapTbl
  [portal_auth_configs table] as PortalCfgTbl
  [breakglass_accounts table] as BreakglassTbl
  [bootstrap.py] as BootstrapSvc
  [portal_auth.py] as PortalAuthSvc
  BootstrapSvc --> BootstrapTbl
  PortalAuthSvc --> PortalCfgTbl
  PortalAuthSvc --> BreakglassTbl
}

[require_authenticated_user()\n(backend/app/security/auth.py)] as Gatekeeper
[SetupWizard.tsx / SetupGate] as WizardUI
[Rest of AccessPilot UI\n(App.tsx, unmodified)] as MainUI

Gatekeeper --> Connector : "1st try — env-var Entra\n(decode_access_token, unchanged)"
Gatekeeper --> PortalAuthSvc : "2nd try — active PortalAuthConfig"
Gatekeeper --> PortalAuthSvc : "3rd try — Break-Glass"

WizardUI --> BootstrapSvc : bootstrap-login
WizardUI --> PortalAuthSvc : configure / activate
MainUI --> Gatekeeper : every API call

note right of IDP
  This is the CSV/Entra/Okta connector
  used for HR onboarding, provisioning,
  birthright policy (Phases 6-11).
  It answers: "what access does a
  USER OF THE COMPANY have?"
end note

note right of PortalCfgTbl
  This answers a different question:
  "who is allowed to log INTO
  AccessPilot's own admin/user portal?"
  Deliberately separate per the user's
  own requirement.
end note

@enduml


' ============================================================================
' Diagram B — First-time setup wizard flow (what SetupWizard.tsx drives)
' ============================================================================
@startuml B_setup_flow
title Phase 12 — First-time Portal Setup Flow

actor Admin
participant "SetupWizard.tsx\n(frontend)" as UI
participant "FastAPI backend" as API
database "Postgres" as DB
participant "Entra / Okta" as IDP

Admin -> UI : opens AccessPilot
UI -> API : GET /api/v1/setup/status
API -> DB : portal_setup_is_needed()\n(env-var Entra configured? OR\nan active PortalAuthConfig exists?)
API --> UI : {needs_setup: true}
note right : Only true on a genuinely\nfresh install. False here\nkeeps the WHOLE existing\napp rendering unchanged.

UI -> Admin : Step 1 — show bootstrap login form
note left of Admin : password was printed\nONCE to the backend's\nstartup log at boot

Admin -> UI : submits admin / <bootstrap password>
UI -> API : POST /setup/bootstrap-login\n{username, password}
API -> DB : verify_bootstrap_login()\n(PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 verify)
API --> UI : {setup_token}\n(HS256 JWT signed with THIS\ncredential row's own session_secret)

UI -> Admin : Step 2 — configure IDP + Break-Glass form
Admin -> UI : idp_type, tenant/client id,\nauthority, break-glass user+pass
UI -> API : POST /setup/configure\nBearer setup_token
API -> DB : create_pending_setup()\n- delete any abandoned pending rows\n- insert PortalAuthConfig (is_active=false)\n- insert BreakGlassAccount (is_active=false,\n  password PBKDF2-hashed)
API --> UI : pending config {id, idp_type, ...}

UI -> Admin : Step 3 — "Test sign-in with Microsoft"
UI -> IDP : loginPopup() via a temporary\nMSAL PublicClientApplication\nbuilt from the PENDING config values
Admin -> IDP : real interactive login
IDP --> UI : real id_token / access_token

UI -> API : POST /setup/activate\nBearer setup_token\n{config_id, test_token}
API -> IDP : fetch JWKS (cached PyJWKClient,\nasyncio.to_thread + 10s timeout —\nsame pattern as the event-loop-freeze fix)
API -> API : validate_token_against_config()\n- verify signature via JWKS\n- check issuer / audience\n- check tenant match
alt token valid
  API -> DB : activate_portal_auth_config()\n- deactivate any other config (defensive)\n- config.is_active = true\n- activate every pending BreakGlassAccount\n- DELETE FROM bootstrap_credentials\n  (self-destruct — its session_secret\n  is gone, so old setup_tokens die too)\n- record_audit(PORTAL_AUTH_CONFIG_ACTIVATED)
  API --> UI : {activated: true}
  UI -> Admin : Step 4 — Done screen
else token invalid / expired setup_token
  API --> UI : 400/401 with error detail
  UI -> Admin : show error, allow retry
end

@enduml


' ============================================================================
' Diagram C — Runtime request authentication: the 3-tier fallback chain
' ============================================================================
@startuml C_auth_fallback
title Every authenticated API call — require_authenticated_user() fallback chain

participant "Browser / API client" as Client
participant "require_authenticated_user()" as Gate
participant "decode_access_token()\n(ORIGINAL, byte-for-byte unchanged)" as Primary
participant "_authenticate_via_portal_config_or_breakglass()" as Fallback
database "Postgres" as DB

Client -> Gate : Authorization: Bearer <token>

Gate -> Primary : try: decode via env-var\nENTRA_TENANT_ID/AUTHORITY
alt env-var Entra validates the token
  Primary --> Gate : AuthenticatedUser
  Gate --> Client : 200 (request proceeds)
else raises AccessPilotError\n(e.g. env-var Entra not configured,\nor token doesn't match it)
  Gate -> Fallback : try fallback(token)
  Fallback -> DB : get_active_portal_auth_config()
  alt an ACTIVE PortalAuthConfig exists
    Fallback -> Fallback : validate_token_against_config()\n(JWKS per idp_type, same\nasyncio.wait_for/to_thread safety)
    alt token valid AND has a VALID_ROLES entry
      Fallback --> Gate : AuthenticatedUser\n(real role from token claims)
      Gate --> Client : 200
    else invalid or no recognized role
      Fallback -> DB : decode_breakglass_token()\n(HS256 verify vs account.session_secret)
    end
  else no active config yet
    Fallback -> DB : decode_breakglass_token()
  end
  alt break-glass token valid
    Fallback --> Gate : AuthenticatedUser\n(subject="breakglass:<id>",\nrole=AccessPilot.Admin)
    Gate --> Client : 200
  else nothing matched
    Fallback --> Gate : None
    Gate --> Client : 401 (the ORIGINAL primary_error,\nunchanged error message)
  end
end

note over Primary, Fallback
  On THIS deployment today: env-var Entra is
  configured and no PortalAuthConfig/BreakGlass
  row exists — every request succeeds at the
  very first "Primary" step, exactly as before
  this phase existed. Steps 2-3 are dead code
  paths for you unless you deliberately run
  the Phase 12 setup flow.
end note

@enduml


' ============================================================================
' Diagram D — Lifecycle of the three new tables
' ============================================================================
@startuml D_lifecycle
title Phase 12 — Credential/Config lifecycle

state "No setup yet" as NoSetup
state "Bootstrap credential exists\n(bootstrap_credentials: 1 row)" as BootstrapActive
state "Setup in progress\n(PortalAuthConfig + BreakGlassAccount\nboth is_active=false)" as Pending
state "Activated\n(PortalAuthConfig.is_active=true,\nBreakGlassAccount.is_active=true,\nbootstrap_credentials: 0 rows — deleted)" as Activated

[*] --> NoSetup
NoSetup --> BootstrapActive : ensure_bootstrap_credential()\ncalled at startup when\nportal_setup_is_needed()==true
BootstrapActive --> BootstrapActive : restart backend\n(idempotent — same\ncredential reused)
BootstrapActive --> Pending : POST /setup/configure\n(create_pending_setup)
Pending --> Pending : POST /setup/configure again\n(old pending rows deleted,\nnew ones inserted)
Pending --> Activated : POST /setup/activate\nsucceeds (real token validated)
Activated --> Activated : normal AccessPilot usage\n(env-var Entra still tried FIRST;\nthis config + break-glass are\nthe fallback safety net)

note right of Activated
  Self-destruct mechanics:
  - bootstrap credential row is gone,
    so any old setup_token JWT (signed
    with ITS session_secret) can never
    verify again — no revocation list needed.
  - Same trick protects break-glass tokens:
    delete the BreakGlassAccount row and
    every token ever signed with its
    session_secret instantly dies too.
end note

@enduml
